{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "The Tally defaults both apps ship (docs/tally.md, ADR 0013): the categories time is sorted into, and the rules that sort it. A category has a stable 'id' that tally_days keeps, a name, a color from the area palette (contracts/design/themes.json) and an emoji. A rule matches an 'app' (an Android package or a Windows executable, the whole name, ignoring case), a window 'title' (contains, ignoring case; Windows only, since Android has no titles) or an editor's 'folder' (its name, ignoring case), on 'android', 'windows' or 'any'. The owner's own rules come first, then these in file order; the first match wins and nothing matched is 'other'. Editors come before the title rules, so a file called youtube.ts is still Coding; browsers have no rule, so their titles decide. tools/check_tally_rules.py keeps the file sound, and contracts/vectors/tally.json pins the matching.",
  "categories": [
    {"id": "coding", "name": "Coding", "color": "blue", "emoji": "💻"},
